README.md
    1→# xxhash
    6→xxhash is a Go implementation of the 64-bit [xxHash] algorithm, XXH64. This is a
    7→high-quality hashing algorithm that is much faster than anything in the Go
    8→standard library.
    10→This package provides a straightforward API:
    12→```
    13→func Sum64(b []byte) uint64
    14→func Sum64String(s string) uint64
    15→type Digest struct{ ... }
    16→    func New() *Digest
    17→```
    19→The `Digest` type implements hash.Hash64. Its key methods are:
    21→```
    22→func (*Digest) Write([]byte) (int, error)
    23→func (*Digest) WriteString(string) (int, error)
    24→func (*Digest) Sum64() uint64
    25→```
    27→The package is written with optimized pure Go and also contains even faster
    28→assembly implementations for amd64 and arm64. If desired, the `purego` build tag
    29→opts into using the Go code even on those architectures.
    31→[xxHash]: https://xxhash.com/
    33→## Compatibility
    …
    35→This package is in a module and the latest code is in version 2 of the module.
    36→You need a version of Go with at least "minimal module compatibility" to use
    37→github.com/cespare/xxhash/v2:
    39→* 1.9.7+ for Go 1.9
    40→* 1.10.3+ for Go 1.10
    41→* Go 1.11 or later
    43→I recommend using the latest release of Go.
    45→## Benchmarks
    …
    47→Here are some quick benchmarks comparing the pure-Go and assembly
    48→implementations of Sum64.
    50→| input size | purego    | asm       |
    51→| ---------- | --------- | --------- |
    52→| 4 B        |  1.3 GB/s |  1.2 GB/s |
    53→| 16 B       |  2.9 GB/s |  3.5 GB/s |
    54→| 100 B      |  6.9 GB/s |  8.1 GB/s |
    55→| 4 KB       | 11.7 GB/s | 16.7 GB/s |
    56→| 10 MB      | 12.0 GB/s | 17.3 GB/s |
    58→These numbers were generated on Ubuntu 20.04 with an Intel Xeon Platinum 8252C
    59→CPU using the following commands under Go 1.19.2:
    61→```
    62→benchstat <(go test -tags purego -benchtime 500ms -count 15 -bench 'Sum64$')
    63→benchstat <(go test -benchtime 500ms -count 15 -bench 'Sum64$')
    64→```
    66→## Projects using this package
    …
    68→- [InfluxDB](https://github.com/influxdata/influxdb)
    69→- [Prometheus](https://github.com/prometheus/prometheus)
    70→- [VictoriaMetrics](https://github.com/VictoriaMetrics/VictoriaMetrics)
    71→- [FreeCache](https://github.com/coocood/freecache)
    72→- [FastCache](https://github.com/VictoriaMetrics/fastcache)
    73→- [Ristretto](https://github.com/dgraph-io/ristretto)
    74→- [Badger](https://github.com/dgraph-io/badger)
